                <pb facs="0241" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12,
                                1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 231.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of dispatch No. 228,
                    concerning settlement extension at Shanghai, I have to report that the amended
                    land regulations fixing the boundaries of the extended international settlement
                    sent up here by the Shanghai consular body for formal approval by the diplomatic
                    corps have been approved by all the corps except the French and Russian
                    ministers, who condition their approval upon the maintenance of the agreement
                    made in 1896 for the extension of both settlements. I suppose this is in
                    retaliation for the British opposition to the small extension now asked for by
                    the French.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
